{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Not Jacob.</b> It will no longer be said that the blessings came to you by cunning and deceit but rather by straightforwardness and open vision, and in the end the Holy One, blessed be He, will reveal Himself to you at Bet El and change your name, and there He blesses you — and there I will be and acknowledge them to you. And this is what is written: ״וַיָּשַׂר אֶל מַלְאָךְ וַיֻּכָל בָּכָה וַיִּתְחַנֵּן לוֹ״ (Hosea 12) — the angel wept and entreated him. And what did he entreat of him? ״בֵּית אֵל יִמְצָאֶנּוּ וְשָׁם יְדַבֵּר עִמָּנוּ״ — wait for me until He speaks with us there. But Jacob refused, and against his will he acknowledged them to him, and this is ״וַיְבָרֶךְ אֹתוֹ שָׁם״ — that he was entreating him to wait for him and he refused." "<b>And with men.</b> Esav and Lavan." "<b>And you will prevail.</b> Over them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:52.093448661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}